On Thu, 11 Aug 2005, Haakon Studebaker wrote:

> A while ago there was a thread about a new version of Patchhack for 3.4.3..
> Cite: http://tinyurl.com/8xtdw
> I went to the sourceforge page and didn't find anything beyond 2002 and I
> was wondering if there has been any progress on the project.

Regarding "the project": PatchHack started as a binary DOS distribution by
me for people who did not want to compile NetHack themselves. Then it was
taken over as a source distribution by Jason Short. Apparently, this
project has since been discontinued, so I again put various patches
together and published a binary. This is currently available for Windows
at http://www.online-club.de/~phlucas/nh.html .

Regarding "progress": I do not know whether nowadays anyone actually uses
PatchHack and what those people would like to have integrated. Thus,
PatchHack has not been updated for a few months.

Anyway, if the binary is not suitable for your needs, you will get any
assistance you need in rgrn if you wish to patch and compile NetHack.

